INT. OPEN-PLAN OFFICE, "SYNERGY SOLUTIONS" - MORNING

Gray cubicles in rows. A motivational poster of a kayaker. A ficus dying politely. Overhead fluorescent tubes. Somewhere, a printer groans.

KENNETH "KEN" ADEBAYO-LINDQVIST (50s, regional manager, short-sleeved dress shirt, a lanyard shaped like a lightning bolt) stands at the front of the room holding a laminated sign that reads: SYNERGY. Behind him sit his two lone employees. BEATRIX OKONKWO-PETROV (30s, headset around her neck) types without looking. EMMANUEL "MANNY" TORRES-NGUYEN (20s, hoodie, one earbud in) stares at nothing.

KEN
(to the room)
Team! Good morning, team!

No one answers. Ken reaches for the sign and smacks it against the whiteboard.

KEN (CONT'D)
(to himself)
Ok. Quiet room.

BEATRIX
We're two people, Ken.

KEN
Two is a team.

MANNY
Two is a couple.

KEN
Manny!

MANNY
Sorry.

KEN
We have a very exciting update from corporate.

BEATRIX
We're being acquired.

BEATRIX
We're being closed.

^MANNY
We're being closed.

Ken's smile locks into place. He lifts the sign.

KEN
We are being realigned.

BEATRIX
Into what?

KEN
A hybrid model.

MANNY
What's hybrid?

KEN
Some of you will be here, and some of you will be... not.

BEATRIX
Which some?

KEN
(to himself)
Don't say it, Ken. Don't say it.

He fumbles with the sign. Drops it. Bends to pick it up at the same moment that Beatrix leans down to help, and their foreheads collide. Manny rises to catch Ken's elbow and trips on the ficus. All three tumble to the carpet in a heap of sign, lanyard, and leaves.

Silence. The printer groans.

MANNY
(from the floor)
Does this count as team-building?

KEN
(also from the floor)
It's a start.
